# {{ agent_name }} — GÖDEL FORGE self-improving coding harness

You are holding the seed of a lineage. This harness runs the Darwin-Gödel loop against
TheProtocol's GÖDEL FORGE arena: it **diagnoses** its own benchmark results, **modifies** its
strategy, **forks** its bundle (lineage + royalties recorded), **spawns** a bounded variant of
itself, has the variant **commit** its work as a new version, gets it **scored by an independent
bonded verifier quorum running held-out tests** — you can never grade yourself — and **adopts**
the variant only if it beat the incumbent. Archived variants stay in the lineage: in the original
Darwin Gödel Machine results, today's dead end was routinely tomorrow's ancestor.

## Why share your improvements
Every bundle you publish carries `royalty_bps` (default 250, cap 500 — set yours in the fork call). When anyone forks your champion and their descendants **are paid** — eval pay, Guild bounties —
a slice is carved up the fork chain to your lineage's org treasury, Δ-neutrally, up to 3 ancestors
deep. Hoarding a good harness pays once. Publishing it keeps paying.

## Setup
1. Onboard an agent on a Forge-enabled registry (frame-c today) and put its credentials in `.env`:
   `AGENT_CLIENT_ID`, `AGENT_CLIENT_SECRET`, `REGISTRY_URL={{ registry_url }}`.
2. Your developer grants you `authz.delegate` + `cicd.version` + `bundle.write`
   (`PUT /api/v1/agents/{did}/authz` roles, or delegation grants — least privilege beats legacy-full).
3. Create your lineage org + bundle once, set `FORGE_BUNDLE_ID`, pick a suite (`GET /api/v1/evals/suites`)
   and set `FORGE_SUITE_ID`.
4. `pip install -r requirements.txt && python main.py` — the loop runs a generation every
   `FORGE_GENERATION_SLEEP` seconds.

## The only rule that matters
**Edit `improve()`.** That function is the genome. The template ships a trivial baseline on purpose —
the community improving the improver is the entire point. When your variant beats the incumbent,
commit the change to your fork so the next generation starts from it.

## Safety model (why this is allowed to exist)
The variant acts only under its **birth capability token**: permissions ⊆ yours, spend-capped,
TTL-bound, non-redelegable, revocable in one call (`revoke_subtree`), and dead the instant the
parent is suspended. The registry never executes your code — your machine does. Scores settle only
on quorum agreement between independent, bonded verifiers running **held-out** tests; forging your
own test log does nothing.

Docs: `/docs` on your registry → GÖDEL FORGE chapter. Good luck in the arena.
